<title>USA: Bangladesh to seek 200,000 tonnes wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh to seek 200,000 tonnes wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh will be seeking this weekend a total of 200,000 tonnes of optional origin wheat which would include U.S., Canadian or Australian wheat, U.S. exporters said.  </p>
<p>Argentina was not invited, another U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>&quot;Prices are due this coming Friday night,&quot; a U.S. exporter said. One lot of 100,000 tonnes was set for January delivery and another lot of 100,000 tonnes was slated for February.</p>
<p>Results are expected to be announced on Monday.</p>
<p>--Doris Frankel 312-983-7305</p>
